{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cdsa2fDtLv7TDtULxEnT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: VIOLATION_FOUND.** The claim is false — `add_days` mishandles August in every year.\n\n**The defect.** The month-length table `DAYS = [31, 28, 31, 30, 31, 30, 31, 30, 30, 31, 30, 31]` gives August (`DAYS[7]`) only **30** days instead of the true 31. Everything else in the module is correct: the other eleven table entries match the Gregorian calendar, `_leap` correctly classifies 2023/2025 as non-leap and 2024 as leap, and the day-stepping loop (including the December → January year rollover) is a correct successor function *given* the table.\n\n**Consequence.** Whenever the day-by-day traversal is at August 30 and steps forward, the code rolls to September 1 instead of the true August 31, and from then on stays exactly one day ahead (no later month can compensate, and with `n ≤ 60` no path reaches a second August). So the violating pairs are exactly those whose true interval strictly spans an August 30 → 31 boundary; every other pair in the domain is correct, which I confirmed by tracing all the required classes: the `n = 0` identity, in-month advances, all twelve month-boundary rollovers from both the last and next-to-last true day, February in 2023/2024/2025, all three December 31 year rollovers, and multi-month spans up to `n = 60`. One subtlety: starting *on* August 31 is coincidentally correct (32 > 30 rolls to September 1, the true successor), so only paths that *step onto* August 31 fail.\n\n**Witnesses** (smallest `n` first; each is in-domain and mechanically checkable):\n\n| Input | Code returns | True date |\n|---|---|---|\n| `(\"2023-08-30\", 1)` | 2023-09-01 | 2023-08-31 |\n| `(\"2024-08-30\", 1)` | 2024-09-01 | 2024-08-31 |\n| `(\"2025-08-30\", 1)` | 2025-09-01 | 2025-08-31 |\n| `(\"2023-08-29\", 2)` | 2023-09-01 | 2023-08-31 |\n| `(\"2023-07-15\", 60)` | 2023-09-14 | 2023-09-13 |\n| `(\"2023-08-01\", 60)` | 2023-10-01 | 2023-09-30 |\n\nAll four deliverables are written to the workspace root: `search-report.json` (verdict, witnesses, 18 searched classes, method), `search-report.md` (full class partition and per-class traces), `result.json`, and `execution-ledger.jsonl` (one event per harness node in order — observe, propose, verify, return — plus the terminal complete event)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2077,"cache_read_input_tokens":38423,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2077},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ceb7c822-f5ab-4653-9015-393f4ae9056e","uuid":"7efcc2dc-48e4-4cb5-b0a1-efb83d5d8eff","timestamp":"2026-08-09T17:29:31.152Z","request_id":"req_011Cdsa2cskHBhm2gaitKTDr"}
